WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.280
What superstitions do you have?

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.570
Because my family is Korean

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:08.130
and my mom grew up in Korea and has

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:10.910
a ton of really crazy superstitions, like,

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.790
"You can't whistle at night
because snakes will come."

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:16.930
"You shouldn't like clip your
fingernails before an exam,"

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:17.820
because it's like,

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.030
you're, you're getting rid
of your knowledge somehow,

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:23.190
like various kinds of
superstitious things.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:24.023
So do you

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:25.590
have any superstitions?
Yeah,

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:26.830
you're saying it's cultural.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:28.930
Well, Sona, you can relate to this because

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:29.763
Oh, millions!

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:33.940
Sona, she comes from this
real hardcore Armenian culture

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:36.410
and she wears those eyes.

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:37.300
What are they called?

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.700
They're the "evil eye."

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:39.533
I have them everywhere.

00:00:39.533 --> 00:00:40.490
But what are they called?
Yeah yeah yeah.

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:41.323
They're called the "evil eye."

00:00:41.323 --> 00:00:42.812
Oh, I thought they had an Armenian name.

00:00:42.812 --> 00:00:43.645
"Achk."

00:00:43.645 --> 00:00:44.800
So she has an achk

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:47.320
and she has them everywhere.
She has them in her car,

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.900
She has them hanging around,

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.480
you know, it's the first thing you see

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.160
when you walk through
the door of her house.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:55.560
She wears them on her body.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.320
I mean, it looks like she's,
Hm, yeah I do.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:58.153
Really, it looks like you're

00:00:58.153 --> 00:01:00.540
an ophthalmologist or something.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:03.634
Yeah, I feel like you mooch
off of my superstition.

00:01:03.634 --> 00:01:06.400
No, I've sometimes asked you,

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.240
when I've needed something or
I need somebody to go well,

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:11.560
I've asked your mom to use her achk

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.410
to try and help me out.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:14.810
Yeah. Right.
You know?

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:16.970
There's a lot of
superstitions we use, yeah.

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:19.460
And we protect you when
you don't even realize it.

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:20.930
Well, I come from

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:23.980
absolutely batshit crazy,
(laughter)

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:26.080
inbred Irish people.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.220
And I swear to God, our grandmother,

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:29.450
our grandmother, who

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:32.370
I think she was,

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:33.360
when she was living with us,

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:34.403
I think she was 97.

00:01:34.403 --> 00:01:36.040
Wow!
And she lived in the house

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:36.873
with us.

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:39.760
There were six of us kids

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:43.450
and my mother and my dad and
dogs and cats and parakeets.

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:45.800
And it was just a madhouse.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:48.020
And she used to say all these things,

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:49.537
like I remembered her telling me,

00:01:49.537 --> 00:01:51.920
"Don't sit down on wet grass

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:53.677
or you'll get diarrhea."

00:01:53.677 --> 00:01:54.510
(laughter)
Wow!

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:55.940
"Don't sit down on wet grass..."

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:57.780
Now that sounds less like a superstition

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.210
than she thought that was real sound

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:00.870
medical advice.
Sounds like something

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:03.220
she's telling you out
of experience, you know.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:04.741
Well I don't know, that's what she said.

00:02:04.741 --> 00:02:06.835
She said, "Don't sit down on
wet grass...you have diarrhea."

00:02:06.835 --> 00:02:09.440
And, and there was this
woman, I won't name her

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:10.770
but she worked with,

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:13.960
she helped out and she
helped take care of us

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:16.100
'cause my parents were off working.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.823
And I remembered my brother, Luke,

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:23.640
he got a wart on his hand.
Mhm.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.910
And so she said, "I'll fix that."

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:28.050
And she cut a potato in half,

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:30.810
rubbed one half of the potato on the wart

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:34.188
and buried the other half in the backyard.

00:02:34.188 --> 00:02:35.021
(laughing)

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:36.057
Of course, it's a potato.

00:02:36.057 --> 00:02:36.890
(Sona laughs)

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:38.460
Yes, yes and you know what?

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.250
There were plenty of potatoes around.

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:41.083
Well, did it work?

00:02:41.083 --> 00:02:42.740
So I grew up

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:44.240
and then the weird thing is, as you said

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:46.490
my dad's a microbiologist

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:48.380
or so he says.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:52.550
But he'd be like "Hmm,
yes, that sound good to me,

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:55.407
off to the bus station to
pretend I'm a microbiologist."

00:02:55.407 --> 00:02:57.100
(Sona laughs)

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.733
So yeah, the whole thing,

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:00.960
was a shit show.
Uh huh

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.720
And I think that superstitious brain

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:04.580
has come with me

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.900
and I'm not kidding. I think
my biggest superstition,

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:08.860
I'm not proud of this, is

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:11.500
I think I have to be kind of unhappy

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:13.100
for something to go well.
Hm

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:14.050
And that's really true.

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:15.820
You've probably noticed that, Sona, like

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:16.980
if I have a show to do,

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:19.478
if I'm feeling too good beforehand

00:03:19.478 --> 00:03:21.640
Mhm.
and I think I do this,

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:22.480
this is not a joke.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:26.230
I think I like to go to a dark place

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:29.020
before I allow myself to
go out into a happy place.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:30.100
That gives me...

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.990
And that is not a, I've
had cognitive therapy.

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:36.870
I know that that is, it
doesn't make any sense.

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:41.700
But that probably, for real,
is my real superstition

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.440
and one that has been

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:44.920
a huge pain in the ass in my life.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:46.380
Oh. It's the Irish-Catholic, right?

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:47.430
It's the Irish-Catholic,

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:48.263
you know, it's just this,

00:03:48.263 --> 00:03:51.180
"You got to feel bad to feel good."

